{"title":"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A triangle has side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/c/94c9cc980f0d47c1d95d6dc57372f375410c0ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/0/530a6d411166475a658b77d8df9f52a0b420f0c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a8026d9abac4fe5835816e026938956312fea7a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"39\" height=\"10\" />, as shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If the perimeter of the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/a/8da2038a882b47e2184ab809431639593cff639b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\text{ cm}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" />, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/958feef2dfce6748bf679ef2a293d0f6e88377c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 3 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 5 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"351\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perimeter\" title=\"Perimeter\">perimeter</a> of a shape is equal to the sum of its side lengths. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/0/ae06c40e28e5022671a8a912a47d2f479d9ac486.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 5 + x = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"117\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fccdaa2b66150ee9e67753e4034c6aaf178c27e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + 8 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"86\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/e/6de86b3a1cb7d6530df81c8c3071c032b591f25c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 12 - 8 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(C) } 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"166\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)\">2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8)</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Answer_Key&amp;act